# Briglia-private Python environment (security plan v24 §7.9.4): the packages the bundled
# skills need. Regenerate the lock with scripts/python_lock.py --regenerate after any change.
# A line is a bare name, optionally with ONE upper-bound cap ("name<version").
openpyxl
python-docx
python-pptx
pillow
formulas
# pymupdf is capped below 2 (owner decision 2026-10-25): 2.x pulls in onnxruntime,
# pymupdf-layout and pymupdf4llm (~460 MB venv), none of which the skills use.
pymupdf<2
weasyprint
# numpy-financial (needed by formulas) is capped below 1.1 (owner decision 2026-11-10): 1.1.0 ships
# compiled wheels for macOS, Linux x86_64 and Windows only, so Linux aarch64 (Raspberry Pi OS 13,
# Debian 13 ARM) with Python >= 3.13 could not install the lock; 1.0.0 is pure Python for every version.
numpy-financial<1.1
